<title>HUNGARY: Philips to build car audio plant in Hungary.</title>
<headline>Philips to build car audio plant in Hungary.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch electronics giant Philips Electronics NV will build a $30 million plant in the northwestern Hungarian city of Gyor to assemble car audio equipment, the company announced.</p>
<p>Philips Hungary director general William van der Vegt told reporters in Gyor that the plant would start by assembling cassette players and would be expanded to other products if the first phase proved successful, Hungarian news agency MTI reported.</p>
<p>The plant will employ 600-800 workers but could go up to 1,000, MTI reported.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom ++ 36 1 327 4040</p>
